The SUSLA Radiologic Technology Program proudly celebrated its Class of 2026 Pinning Ceremony on recently at Riverview Hall. Eleven graduates were pinned by family and friends, culminating two years of academic and clinical preparation.
&nbsp;
The Class of 2026 achieved a 100% pass rate on the program Exit Examination, with five graduates already passing the National Board Examination with scores of 90 or higher. The program proudly anticipates a 100% National Board Examination pass rate for the class.
&nbsp;
Dr. Sharon F. Green, Founding Director, delivered an inspiring message encouraging graduates to remain Resilient, Respectful, and Ready for the Reward.
The program extends sincere appreciation to our Clinical Education Centers, alumni, community partners, administration, faculty, staff, students, and families for their continued support, with special thanks to Mr. Matthew Valliere, CEO of CareSouth Health, for his generous contribution to the Class of 2026.
&nbsp;
Kudos to the Radiologic Technology faculty for another successful year, and&nbsp;<span class="marka4mzjpbxt uM2yb" data-markjs="true">congratulations</span>&nbsp;to the Class of 2026!&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Resilient. Respectful. Ready for the Reward.
&nbsp;
